{"kind":"report","text":"The exact seven-file counting preparation is supported with limits. No blocking declaration defect was found. This is preparatory feedback, not formal source approval or permission to land.\n\nThe reviewed head is 10eb735ad773c491969168b1c8c5184b781f3e18, tree fed7f6585361095e40b12cf57d1b5ecaf67bae3f, against main 9d7e4c2777ea8d35441b4a9d79b407cd701065fa. Corrected feedback request d63309420a5e0d50fac2e014626ea86f75d396c8 and checker promise 4f9f97efea27aa62be3eed26efe2f5c4b4586ec1 replace only the earlier review-task metadata. The ordinary Git implementation 8d319/09fd and the full counting 4073/durability 578 obligations remain open. Later 32ad integration and e10 domain controls are different, unreviewed source.\n\nRoot and two independent readers each freshly read all seven bodies and complete native U3 diffs: 14 units, 22 bounded displays, 86,588 bytes and 850 LF. The sorted, gap-free native byte/hash/UTF8/EOF audit passed with exit0, SHA256 504629489f597ddfc2cc924a3c6030416c0491e2594efbc10a962f2a7c8d4421. Root read all four helper seals, including the metadata correction; seal and eleven fresh native partial spans (17,115 bytes) passed a separate audit, SHA256 d068169ae6decfe283394f122154e94a250137898bb50795b466a74bed1bc86d. Partial dependencies and supplements are excluded from primary coverage.\n\nThe declaration uses existing restricted@1 forms. It opens an untimed configuration, then requires the controller's Initialize to open the board. Complete ordered native participant IDs and exact MemberRefs constrain proposed rosters; the scope checks number, generation, serial and successor before copying values. Current-speaker Leave changes serial while preserving the unfinished number; non-current Leave preserves the turn. Empty replacement pauses and clears the optional next binding. CancelTurn requires the controller and actual current speaker. Reset fences old completions even when serial/number repeat; expiry pauses without advancing the count. There are no child definitions, durable sends, outside operations, sorting or app-specific Core counter.\n\nFresh native source corroborates complete sameSet membership/order checks, ascending page order, opening ID equal to entry sequence, MemberRef signer checks and conditions evaluated before effects. This matters for Leave: replacing the speaker cannot change which conditional effects should apply in that entry.\n\nThe four authored model fixtures make useful distinctions: three-to-four roster progression, wrong speaker and order, exact-envelope duplicate versus stale fresh fields, nonzero current/non-current departures, empty roster, known roster-refusal correction, reset generation, exact-deadline due/drain and retained refolding. Actual tests, types and semantic-control results remain producer-attributed; checker executed none. Fixture grants give every actor all declared actions. These fixtures therefore test domain party/field guards, not real enrollment, role denial, authority windows or revocation. Refolding memory is not a Worker restart or replay-of-judgments proof.\n\nP3: definition.test.ts:52–59 checks parsed equality after trimEnd, rather than the exact compact canonical file and one trailing LF. Add that byte assertion within the existing canonical-definition fixture. The current file is correct: independent literal JSON/hash checks reproduce sha256:435d9f5745048183d3cf0392ce909cd76909fd69ee368dfc57e142ba96af1d09. Root pin audit passed, SHA256 f753a1d568309b4e3fe852a0b8de4e32d88f4960eb9938bc64259f9f4cc444f7. One initial local check guessed the wrong domain tag and failed before any PASS; the actual native artroom-definition-1 tag was then read and checked. No source pin mismatch was found.\n\nThe frozen model also lacks independent wrong-controller, duplicate self-Join and forged MemberRef controls. Planner23 already routes these into existing fixtures on the successor; do not count those later changes as reviewed here. The final source